id: pm-web-t2oi
title: List pm-swarm in the package catalog as an unreleased fleet package
description: "Add the public pm-swarm workflow extension with commands and schema capabilities, seven documented swarm commands and GitHub links; keep installation unavailable until publication. Cover the catalog, fleet roster, snapshot, UI and compiled HTTP behavior."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: catalog,pm-swarm
created_at: "2026-10-15T21:36:06.580Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T22:33:42.624Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Swarm metadata and unreleased installation boundary are covered by regression tests; behavioral revert proof fails; npm and Bun release gates pass at unchanged thresholds.
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T21:36:35.897Z",codex-agent,"Read pm-swarm package.json pm block and manifest.json on feat/swarm: workflow product extension with commands and schema capabilities. Keep the manifest summary unchanged in the fleet receipt while explicitly verifying the requested longer catalog display text. Add seven command paths, public links, unreleased UI and HTTP installation checks, roster coverage and behavioral revert proof. No runtime dependency changes are needed."
  "2026-10-15T21:38:39.225Z",codex-agent,"npm view pm-swarm version --json returned E404, confirming npmPublished false despite publishConfig intent. The complete roster now contains 25 public identities: 24 extensions (17 published, seven unreleased) plus native Rust. Initial broader local catalog checks detected partial sibling-worktree discovery and separate ADO/Jev upstream metadata drift. Full gates will use a standalone clone of the candidate commit, matching CI snapshot coverage without changing thresholds or tests. The UI test asserts the existing i18n badge attribute because this unit harness does not load translations."
  "2026-10-15T21:39:09.511Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: removed only the pm-swarm entry from PACKAGE_CATALOG, leaving all tests and fixtures intact. node --test --test-name-pattern pm-swarm test/catalog.test.ts test/catalog-ui.test.ts executed two tests with 0 passed and 2 assertion failures (missing catalog entry), zero skips and no module-load errors. Restored the exact source bytes; the same command passes 2/2. Separate canonical ADO/Jev metadata drift is tracked by pm-web-5hdb."
  "2026-10-15T21:40:19.493Z",codex-agent,"The feat/swarm branch was merged and removed during verification; re-reading manifest.json on main confirms the same summary and commands/schema capabilities. The implementation uses the requested curated card description, and source/snapshot tests assert both exact descriptions. Built catalog acceptance passes 1/1 against a real scratch tracker."
  "2026-10-15T21:44:56.975Z",codex-agent,"Standalone focused catalog/UI/built/discovery acceptance passes 28/28 after the normal build. The initial pm-linked HTTP attempt ran concurrently with a direct HTTP acceptance and reached the existing 300000ms per-test deadline: 1 passed, 1 canceled and 1 failed (spawn ENOTDIR after timeout cleanup). Preserve this as failed evidence; the linked source/UI command passed 2/2. No deadline or release threshold is changed. Full release gates and a non-overlapping linked HTTP retry are pending."
  "2026-10-15T21:47:12.132Z",codex-agent,"Direct node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test test/catalog-install-e2e.test.ts passes 3/3, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Built scenario 268798.261578ms; source scenario 241200.463079ms. Both list all 25 identities, install and run published Presets, and refuse pm-swarm installation with HTTP 409 without changing settings. This contrasts with the preserved overlapping pm-linked timeout in pm-web-qdhx. Full npm/Bun release verification remains pending."
  "2026-10-15T22:02:08.187Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check PASSED on dc63489 in a standalone clone with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. Coverage suite 601/601, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo; all 37 configured source files reported; S/L 90.94%, B 81.18%, F 94.17% at unchanged 90/90/79/92 thresholds. Capacity 1/1; production audit zero vulnerabilities; packed current/minimum npm/Bun consumers 4/4; changelog, release-date and publish-attestation checks pass. Full-suite HTTP scenarios pass built 254189.02205ms and source 188243.174177ms at unchanged 300000ms deadlines, supplying a successful rerun after the preserved pm-linked timeout. Bun release gate is running sequentially."
  "2026-10-15T22:32:59.346Z",codex-agent,"Full bun run release:check PASSED on unchanged implementation dc63489 with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration: 601/601 tests; zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo; all 37 configured sources; S/L 90.91%, B 81.14%, F 94.17% at unchanged 90/90/79/92 thresholds. Capacity 1/1, packed current/minimum npm/Bun consumers 4/4, zero production vulnerabilities, and changelog/release-date/publish-attestation checks all pass. Built/source HTTP scenarios pass at 166200.268747ms and 189986.526424ms with unchanged deadlines. Both release gates are green; preserve the earlier pm-linked timeout under pm-web-qdhx. Remaining changes are tracker receipts only; no items are closed."
